{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfwdb6hGd5H6LSK85mZtV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I didn't open the dashboard or wait for the rule to run, so I haven't seen either one working.\n\n**Data:** The data view uses `timestamp` as its time field. `response` is a string, so I matched it through `response.keyword`. Other fields I used or noted:\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `geo.src`\n- `geo.dest`\n- `clientip`\n- `machine.os`\n- `agent`\n- `url`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-904ab573 Web logs overview\" has 5 panels. Open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-904ab573-web-logs-overview-ceda7d99f1db. The panels are:\n- Total requests (single number)\n- Requests over time (line)\n- Responses by status code (pie)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar)\n- Top source countries (table)\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-904ab573 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It looks back 5 minutes and fires when more than 10 documents have a `response.keyword` matching `5xx`. The rule has no actions attached, so a firing is recorded but nothing is sent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":20336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159},"output_tokens":415,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"246af32e-0b2c-452b-9867-63e82b21b47e","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:27:20.042Z","request_id":"req_011Cfwdb6VNGsTzDyH6SK4tz"}
